Cell["6. Clipping the gradient by its norm", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e8366319-1057-487e-bc15-e9716b5198c7"],

Cell["\<\
LSTMs rarely have vanishing gradients but can have exploding ones. For each \
batch the paper computes the norm s of the whole gradient g (all parameters \
together) and, if s > 5, rescales g to 5 g / s (Section 3.4).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ab1190cb-bbbf-40eb-ba6a-3a678717120f"],

Cell["s = \[LeftDoubleBracketingBar]g\[RightDoubleBracketingBar]\:2082 ;   if \
s > 5 :  g \[LeftArrow] 5 g / s", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"aae2a581-7ab6-\
462d-8243-d1cdb7570a84"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "after clipping, the norm is 5 (it was 13.8)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5ee77268-915b-448c-9442-651ebecd60a8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the direction is unchanged: cosine(g, clipped g) = 1"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"57a65070-195c-4a79-a716-bed3c4c9d42d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "clamping each component to [\[Minus]1, 1] instead turns the direction \
(cosine 0.915)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c229640c-6afa-4a73-9029-cd96ebd63a07"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "a small gradient is left alone"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"25b59d76-3339-4424-9fa1-2da1ff7d20f5"],

Cell["7. The learning-rate schedule", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"56bb4af0-73c9-4152-8c05-3897c39efeaf"],

Cell["\<\
Plain stochastic gradient descent without momentum, learning rate 0.7. After \
5 epochs the rate is halved every half epoch; training stops after 7.5 \
epochs. Batches hold 128 sentences (Section 3.4).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2fd9eb3a-771e-4965-bcca-2f2a5367de4e"],

