 "0.7 up to epoch 5, then 0.35, 0.175, \[Ellipsis] down to 0.7/32 in the last \
half epoch"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2da037d5-ade6-4e40-806e-8c08c6c72354"],

Cell["8. Beam search", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"d413ddd1-49c4-4760-9907-f6a1f263f527"],

Cell["\<\
The decoder is run left to right, keeping the B most likely partial \
translations. Each is extended by every word; the B best of all the \
extensions are kept. A hypothesis that ends in <EOS> leaves the beam and \
joins the finished list. The paper finds that even B = 1 works well and that \
B = 2 gives most of the benefit (Section 3.2).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f6c9f423-d135-4a21-9e76-828c3e3bb2fa"],

Cell["\<\
Toy model: the first word is A (0.6) or B (0.4). After A the model hesitates \
(A, B: 0.35; <e>: 0.3); after B it almost always stops (<e>: 0.95). Greedy \
decoding takes A and is trapped; a beam of width 2 keeps B alive.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"60340d71-2da8-41cc-91e4-6b75217b99a1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"width\"\>", "\<\"best output\"\>", "\<\"probability\"\>"},
    {"1", 
     TemplateBox[{
      "\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"A\"", "\"A\"", "\"A\"", "\"A\"", "\"A\"", 
       "\"A\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"], 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"0.00315\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       0.0031513124999999983`,
       AutoDelete->True],
      NumberForm[#, 3]& ]},
    {"2", 
     TemplateBox[{"\[ThinSpace]", "\" \"", "\"B\"", "\"<e>\""},
      "RowWithSeparators"], 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"0.38\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       0.38,
       AutoDelete->True],
      NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxBackground->{"Columns" -> {{None}}, "Rows" -> {
       GrayLevel[0.85]}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"37b388cd-f07a-4667-9fb2-f841fb8778dc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the beam of width 2 finds 'B <e>' with probability 0.38"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"70f6ccaf-159a-4ec3-affe-fdf05fca7bb7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "greedy decoding (width 1) ends with a less likely output"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e0c9e3a0-1402-483c-9483-1284e9930e0b"],

Cell["9. The parameter count of the paper's model", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"12aff64b-0763-4e48-9c7f-975cb42cabea"],

Cell["\<\
An LSTM layer with nIn inputs and n cells has four gates, each with \
n\[Times]nIn input weights, n\[Times]n state weights and n biases: 4(n\
\[CenterDot]nIn + n\.b2 + n).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d884ff93-904d-4b6e-92e5-3355b4797cc3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
    {"\<\"source embeddings 160,000 \[Times] 1000\"\>", 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"160,000,000\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       160000000,
       Editable->False],
      NumberForm[#, DigitBlock -> 3]& ]},
    {"\<\"target embeddings 80,000 \[Times] 1000\"\>", 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"80,000,000\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       80000000,
       Editable->False],
      NumberForm[#, DigitBlock -> 3]& ]},
    {"\<\"encoder: 4 LSTM layers of 1000 cells\"\>", 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"32,016,000\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       32016000,
       Editable->False],
      NumberForm[#, DigitBlock -> 3]& ]},
    {"\<\"decoder: 4 LSTM layers of 1000 cells\"\>", 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"32,016,000\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       32016000,
       Editable->False],
      NumberForm[#, DigitBlock -> 3]& ]},
    {"\<\"softmax 80,000 \[Times] 1000 + 80,000\"\>", 
     TagBox[
      InterpretationBox[
       StyleBox["\<\"80,080,000\"\>",
        ShowStringCharacters->False],
       80080000,
       Editable->False],
      NumberForm[#, DigitBlock -> 3]& ]},
    {
     StyleBox["\<\"total\"\>",
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold], 
     StyleBox[
      TagBox[
       InterpretationBox[
        StyleBox["\<\"384,112,000\"\>",
         ShowStringCharacters->False],
        384112000,
        Editable->False],
       NumberForm[#, DigitBlock -> 3]& ],
      StripOnInput->False,
      FontWeight->Bold]}
   },
   AutoDelete->False,
   GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {Left, Right}},
   GridBoxFrame->{"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"29bc8751-9215-4ccc-ad1c-368c522ddbd5"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the formula agrees with Wolfram's count for an LSTM layer with 4 inputs and \
6 cells (264)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e2faf427-8b82-4b6b-b621-a783608d5730"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["PASS  ",
  FontWeight->Bold,
  FontColor->RGBColor[0, 0.5, 0]],
 "the total is 384,112,000: the paper's '384M parameters' (Section 3.4)"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"21bb1817-4591-46c8-b4da-da5b742d5d86"],

Cell["Where this is used in TensorNets", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"374a6a43-2892-422c-8901-06a92cc6ba53"],

Cell["\<\
tnParserNet is a transformer rather than an LSTM (Lesson 3), but three ideas \
come from this paper: an encoder\[Dash]decoder that reads the whole input \
before writing, beam search over the decoder, and clipping the gradient by \
its norm.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b9e39298-46fc-4170-88b4-4de566a92da2"],

